FoMni-1 0.4 BETA – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-fomni tag v0.4
(commit 6ecd227013cc18def0e89d035b3760eb268b342b; source: https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-fomni/archive/6ecd227013cc18def0e89d035b3760eb268b342b.tar.gz).
GPL-3.0-only. FoMni by Charles Vestal, on X0X's and Felucca's platform: Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments (the platform parts).
Its rhythm patterns, waves, drum sounds and the strum plate's voicing come from Chordian by Jan125 (CC0 1.0); the screen reader's announce.c: MPL-2.0; the UI face Barlow Semi Condensed is
rasterised in (OFL 1.1): FoMni's LICENSING.md and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file. Omnichord is a trademark of Suzuki Musical Instrument Corporation. The JieLi SDK files of
FoMni's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/fomni_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as FoMni's own browser emulator does (web/emu/omni_web.c, host/omni_host.c)
and adds the device's storage.c on the flash image, the USB SysEx path (the screen reader, ota.c's identity handshake) and USB MIDI out; the hardware stand-ins are the emulator's:
keys/LEDs/LCD, the MASTER pot, NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, USB = always configured, no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no updater and no USB boot (ota.c answers the identity
handshake only), the default panel map (no hardware calibration). Compiled with WASI SDK clang.

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
The complete corresponding source of this build is https://github.com/charlesvestal/fm1-fomni at commit 6ecd227013cc18def0e89d035b3760eb268b342b
together with FM-1 Companion's build script tools/build_sims.py and the glue tools/studio/fomni_studio.c. A tarball of exactly this commit
(fm1-fomni-6ecd227013cc18def0e89d035b3760eb268b342b.tar.gz, made with tools/make_source_tarballs.py) is attached to every
FM-1 Companion release that ships this build: https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/releases
Written offer: for at least three years after the last release that ships this build, the maintainers of
FM-1 Companion will give anyone a copy of that corresponding source on request (https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/issues),
free of charge apart from the cost of physically performing the distribution.
